From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Mon, 14 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: name the seat of an opponent-field place prompt at n >
 2

The place mask has one high half for "the opponent". With more than two
duelists the message did not say which one, and the answer check accepted
any living seat.

The SelectPlace process gets a target seat (default DUELIST_NONE, the old
behaviour). The callers that offer the zones of another field pass the owner
of that field: MoveToField and Special Summon (move_to_field, two sites),
SSet to another field (SpellSetGroup), Duel.SelectFieldZone (the bound
opponent of the link, else the next living opponent) and Duel.SelectDisableField
(the next living duelist in turn order). The other callers offer own zones only.

At n > 2, when the mask offers a zone of the other field and the target is
named, the core writes MSG_HINT type 0xF0 (HINT_PLACE_SEAT, player = the
prompted seat, data = the target seat) right before MSG_SELECT_PLACE or
MSG_SELECT_DISFIELD. A high half answer must name the target seat exactly,
else MSG_RETRY. With no target seat the old rule stays. The simple AI and
skipped-seat answer uses the target seat.

SelectDisableField and SelectFieldZone offer the zones of that one seat only.
SelectDisableField names the next living duelist in turn order, because the
EFFECT_DISABLE_FIELD code binds the high half of its value to that seat. The
zones that are offered are the zones that get disabled. It used the next seat
even when dead. It now skips the opponent zones when nobody else lives or that
seat is on the same team. SelectFieldZone uses the bound opponent, as the
reads with 1-tp do.

n == 2 is unchanged: no hint, the same rule, the same bytes.

